  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1974-p26.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Because \\[ 30^4=2^4\\cdot3^4\\cdot5^4, \\] a divisor independently chooses each of three exponents from \\(0,\\) \\(1,\\) \\(2,\\) \\(3,\\) \\(4.\\) There are \\(5^3=125\\) divisors. Excluding \\(1\\) and \\(30^4\\) leaves \\(125-2=123.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Factor \\(30^4\\) into powers of \\(2,\\) \\(3,\\) and \\(5\\)",
        "Choose each prime exponent independently from \\(0\\) through \\(4,\\) then remove two divisors"
      ],
